      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, actually, initially I was thinking the sleep mask would take care of it, but it wasn\u0027t, I kept getting garbage printed to the screen when the clock speed changed. The problem is that data can still be in the TX FIFO when the sleep mask is cleared. As for the buffer empty, Randall makes a good point that if the flow control XOFF character is sent, then we will stop sending data, and clear the sleep mask, but when the XON is sent we will miss it if we are using the low speed clock.",
